course: dictionary
lesson: 12702
title: Keep going: doggedly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Doggedly» tells you how someone does something. It means in a stubborn, determined way, without giving up, even when the job is hard. You can hear the word «dog» inside it: a dog that has found a scent will keep following it, and will not let go.
explain: «The explorers trudged doggedly through the snow, one cold step at a time.» The snow is deep and the wind is cold, so the explorers are tired. The word doggedly tells you they did not stop. They kept going.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «The explorers trudged in a determined way, not giving up, through the snow». It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Stubborn can be a bad thing, but here it is a good thing: keeping going is praised.
fact: «Doggedly» is an adverb, so it tells you how an action is done.
fact: «Doggedly» means in a determined way, not giving up even when it is hard.
fact: «Doggedly» is often used with words like «worked», «walked» and «refused».
fact: Scientists, explorers and athletes often work doggedly to reach their goals.
fact: Context clue: if the sentence describes tiredness, rain or failure, and the person still carries on, the word is probably doggedly.
exercise: «The explorers trudged doggedly through the snow.» What does doggedly mean? | Sleepily, with eyes closed | *In a determined way, not giving up | Happily, singing a song | Quickly and carelessly
exercise: «Mia doggedly practised her times tables every night until she knew them all.» What does doggedly show about Mia? | She was very quick and finished first | *She kept trying, even when it was hard | She was bored and stopped | She forgot her times tables
exercise: Which word has nearly the same meaning as doggedly? | sadly | *determinedly | slowly | quickly
test: «The scientist doggedly tested each idea, even when every test failed.» What does doggedly tell you about the scientist? | *The scientist kept testing, without giving up | The scientist tested only once, very fast | The scientist gave up after the first failure | The scientist felt bored and sleepy
test: Which sentence uses doggedly well? | She doggedly ate her lunch and fell asleep | They doggedly left the park as soon as it started to rain | He doggedly won the race in one second flat without trying | *She doggedly climbed the hill in the rain, step by step
exam: «She doggedly kept reading, even though the book was hard.» What does doggedly mean here? | Quickly, to finish the book fast | *Determinedly, refusing to give up | Loudly, so everyone could hear | Sadly, because the book was hard
